{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And YHWH Elohim built.</b> A full name over a full world: just as it says of man ״וייצר ה׳ אלהים״ — a full name over a full world — and he includes the female, and the power of the female is hidden within him, so too the female includes the male, and the power of the male is hidden within her. And this is what is written (Genesis 46:15): ״אלה בני לאה אשר ילדה ליעקב״ — it attributes the sons to the female, to show that the power of the male is hidden away in the female. And this is (Leviticus 12:2): ״אשה כי תזריע וילדה זכר״. And the attribution of the female to the male is what is written (Genesis 46:15): ״ואת דינה בתו״, to show that the power of the female is hidden away in the male." "<b>And from this</b> you will find two utterances in the creation of man and Chavvah, and they are among the ten particular utterances that you will find in the account of Creation, besides בראשית, which is a general utterance. And these two utterances are: ״ויאמר אלהים נעשה אדם״, and ״ויאמר ה׳ אלהים לא טוב היות האדם לבדו אעשה לו עזר כנגדו״. And understand this: the utterance concerning the creation of Chavvah is the tenth utterance." "<b>And there are</b> those who count eighteen utterances — five in the first three days and five in the last three — and according to this the utterance ״הנה נתתי לכם״ would not be included among them. But the principle for us is that בראשית is an utterance, and ״נעשה אדם״ is the ninth, and the utterance ״לא טוב״ is the tenth, and the utterance ״פרו ורבו״ is not included among them, nor is ״הנה נתתי לכם״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:09:38.568294846Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}